# =============================================================================
# .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
#   Git tracks every file in your project folder unless you tell it not to.
#   This file lists files and folders Git should IGNORE, so they are never
#   committed or pushed to GitHub.
#
#   We ignore things that are:
#     1. SECRET:        passwords and API keys (.env)
#     2. RE-CREATABLE:  installed packages and build output (node_modules/, dist/)
#     3. PERSONAL:      OS and editor junk that differs per computer
#
# HOW IT WORKS:
#   - Each line is a pattern.
#   - Lines starting with # are comments.
#   - A trailing slash (folder/) matches a folder.
#   - * is a wildcard: *.log matches every file ending in .log
#   - ! un-ignores something: !.env.example
#
# TIP: Already committed a file by mistake? Adding it here won't remove it.
#      Run: git rm --cached <file>   and then commit.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# Installed packages can be HUGE (hundreds of MB). Anyone can reinstall them
# with `npm install` using package.json, so there's no need to commit them.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnp/
.pnp.js


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment variables (SECRETS!)
# .env holds real API keys and passwords. NEVER commit it.
# .env.example is a safe template with fake values, so we keep it.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# Generated automatically from your source code. Rebuild it anytime.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
out/
coverage/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# Debug logs are created while running the app. They're noisy and personal.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating system files
# Your computer creates these automatically. They're useless to other people.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Linux
*~


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and IDEs
# Personal editor settings. Note: we do NOT ignore .vscode/settings.json,
# because shared team settings are useful. We only ignore personal extras.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI agent local files
# Claude Code can store PERSONAL settings here. The shared .claude/CLAUDE.md
# is still committed so the whole team gets the same AI instructions.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Temporary files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
